        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buying a Treadmill at Sam’s Club</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Warehouse-club treadmill purchases go wrong in predictable ways. These four matter most.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming the name means the current model</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">NordicTrack has used names like Commercial 1250 for several generations with different belts, motors and weight limits. Check the belt size and capacity on the Sam’s listing against the current manufacturer figures before buying.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing a non-member price</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Several Sam’s treadmill listings show their real price only when you sign in. Comparing the price a non-member sees, or a crossed-out "was" price, with another retailer’s delivered price gives the wrong answer.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Relying on "return at any time" without reading the item</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Sam’s general policy does not name treadmills, and electronics have a 90-day limit. Read the item page or ask Member Services, keep the box, and plan how you would get a 300 lb machine back to a club.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
